# NOCA -- Docker Compose settings
#
# NOT an env_file layer. NOCA_DATA_ROOT is interpolated by Compose itself and
# must live in the project-root .env; the rest are container/entrypoint knobs the
# sample stack passes through `environment:`.
#
# Reference: docs/CONFIG.md -- layer map: docs/ENV_LAYERS.md

# Host path prepended to the bind-mounted data directories (problem statements,
# test cases, the mailer's mbox log, Caddy's access log). PostgreSQL and Valkey
# use named volumes and are unaffected.
#
# Keep this at `.` unless you also update scripts/backup_noca.sh: that script
# archives problem_statements, problem_testcases, and email_log relative to the
# project directory and does not read this variable, so pointing the mounts
# elsewhere backs up empty directories without reporting the mismatch.
NOCA_DATA_ROOT=.

# UID that processes run as inside their containers
PUID=1000

# Primary GID that processes run as inside their containers
PGID=100

# GID of the host's docker group, added to the autojudge container so it can reach
# the mounted Docker socket. `getent group docker | cut -d: -f3` on the judge host.
DOCKER_GID=989

# Set to true to seed the built-in language definitions into the database on startup
NOCA_SEED_LANGUAGES=false

# Max seconds a worker (autojudge/rating/aiassistant) waits for the schema to be
# migrated by web/arena before its entrypoint gives up (default 300)
NOCA_WAIT_FOR_MIGRATIONS_TIMEOUT=300
